      "message": "It\u0027s Scenario 2. You tell Chrome to initialize the webgpu-on-webgpu backend.\n\nYou can run your app with little overhead (an extra webgpu passthrough layer + some id tracking (id++, put in a map))\n\nYou can turn on recording during mid-exection.\n\nFor the example, when you are after 8, if buffer is referenced, its state is captured, including its mapState. So the snapshot buffer should have a unmap state.\n\nDoes this sound good?",
