      "writtenOn": "2025-08-06T17:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just want to be clear, It doesn\u0027t seem like the solution can be\n\n1. start capture\n2. make a copy of all resource\n3. record which resources were used\n4. serialize only those resources that were used\n\nStep 1 above \u003d out of memory\n\nIt feels like it potentially needs to be\n\n1. start capture\n2. When a resource is used, if we need its content, serialize that content immediately (read it, put on the disk, not in memory)\n\nGrabbing the content when it\u0027s known to be needed is a very different pattern than capture up front. Maybe the current code is fine if all it\u0027s doing is assigning an id to every resource but not actually grabbing content. But then you\u0027re still left with tracking separately which resources are used. Is it better to track that separately or is it better to (has id \u003d used, doesn\u0027t have id \u003d not used)?",
